{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q022_colg_crya_remote_homology","answer":"In SCOPe 2.04, the ColG collagen-binding domain of 1nqd (d1nqda_; also d1nqdb_) was b.23.2.1: the collagen-binding family and superfamily in the CUB-like fold. The Cry3A C-terminal/domain-III region d1dlca1 (A:500–644) was b.18.1.3 in the galactose-binding-domain-like fold and superfamily. They therefore shared only the all-beta class, which did not imply homology. In current public SCOPe 2.08 (latest periodic update 2.08-2026-08-16), ColG has been reassigned to the galactose-binding-domain-like superfamily as the distinct collagen-binding family b.18.1.36; Cry3A remains b.18.1.3. Thus they now share superfamily b.18.1, supporting probable remote common ancestry, but remain different families. The chain-B ColG copy is now d1nqdb1 (B:893–1008), with residues 891–892 separately treated as an artifact domain.

The structural case is a conserved compact all-beta, two-sheet beta-sandwich scaffold despite very weak sequence similarity. SCOPe explicitly cites PMID 17977833 as describing likely homology among ColG d1nqdb_, the Cry4Ba C-terminal domain d1w99a3, and the C-terminal domain of C. perfringens enterotoxin d2quoa_. Stored FATCAT evidence supplies a quantitative bridge: 1nqdA itself has no stored hits because its 99.16%-identical representative is 1nqjA; that representative aligns to Cry4Ba d1w99a3 (also family b.18.1.3) with P=0.00395 and RMSD 2.52 Å across a 94-residue ColG region, despite only 2.5% identity. Because Cry4Ba and Cry3A are members of the same SCOPe family, this supports a shared ancestral scaffold with Cry3A, although it is not a direct 1nqd–1dlc alignment.

Functionally, these are C-terminal ligand-targeting modules attached to otherwise different bacterial effector proteins: ColG’s domain binds collagen and is observed with Ca2+, whereas Cry domain III contributes receptor/ligand recognition and toxin specificity. Their common role as adaptable surface-binding modules is consistent with divergence from an ancestral binding domain, but functional analogy alone is not proof. The superfamily assignment must not be used to transfer collagen binding, Ca2+-site residues, Cry receptor specificity, insecticidal activity, or catalytic function between them. Likewise, one may use the other family only as a remote fold/topology template; domain boundaries, alignments, side-chain positions, and ligand-binding sites require independent sequence/structure and biochemical evidence. The representative-based FATCAT result must also remain labeled as evidence from 1nqjA and Cry4Ba, not as a direct measurement on 1nqd and Cry3A.","evidence_used":["get_scop_service_info — /api/v1/, /api/v1/releases/current","get_scop_pdb_entry — /api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd, /api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd/domains, /api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc, /api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc/domains, /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd, /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd/domains, /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc, /api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc/domains","compare_scop_domains — /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/homology, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/homology, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/homology, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/homology","get_scop_node — /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607/parents, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607/annotations, /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607/homology","get_scop_chain_hits — /api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqdA/structure-hits?limit=100, /api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqjA/structure-hits?limit=100","search_scop — /api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=17977833&mode=token&limit=50"]}]}
